From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] msi: a per-user package registers its classes in the user's classes (9264)

RegisterClassInfo, RegisterProgIdInfo, RegisterExtensionInfo,
RegisterMIMEInfo and their Unregister actions wrote through
HKEY_CLASSES_ROOT whatever the package's context. Windows Installer writes a
per-machine package's to HKLM\Software\Classes and a per-user package's to
HKCU\Software\Classes. Here a per-user package's classes went to the
machine's when it ran elevated (seen by every user), and, since 9263
refuses a standard user's new HKCR key as Windows does, would have gone
nowhere when it ran as the user. They now go to HKCU\Software\Classes for
any context but the machine's.

Gate: test/msiperuser-gate.sh (a per-user package with an extension,
ProgId and verb, added with msibuild: in the user's classes, not the
machine's; gone after uninstall). Mutant: SG_MUTANT_MSI_USER_CLASSES_MACHINE.
---
--- a/dlls/msi/classes.c
+++ b/dlls/msi/classes.c
@@ -42,6 +42,33 @@
 
 WINE_DEFAULT_DEBUG_CHANNEL(msi);
 
+/* Stained Glass OS (wine-sg 9264): where a package registers its classes, ProgIds, extensions and MIME
+ * types: a per-machine install in the machine's (HKEY_CLASSES_ROOT, HKLM\Software\Classes), a per-user
+ * install in the user's, HKCU\Software\Classes, as Windows Installer does. Everything went through
+ * HKEY_CLASSES_ROOT, which put a per-user install's classes in the machine's when it ran elevated, and
+ * nowhere once a standard user's new key there is refused (9263). */
+static HKEY classes_root = HKEY_CLASSES_ROOT;
+
+static HKEY enter_classes_root( MSIPACKAGE *package )
+{
+    HKEY old = classes_root, user;
+
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_MSI_USER_CLASSES_MACHINE
+    if (package->Context != MSIINSTALLCONTEXT_MACHINE &&
+        !RegCreateKeyExW( HKEY_CURRENT_USER, L"Software\\Classes", 0, NULL, 0, KEY_ALL_ACCESS, NULL, &user, NULL ))
+        classes_root = user;
+    else
+#endif
+        classes_root = HKEY_CLASSES_ROOT;
+    return old;
+}
+
+static void leave_classes_root( HKEY old )
+{
+    if (classes_root != HKEY_CLASSES_ROOT) RegCloseKey( classes_root );
+    classes_root = old;
+}
+
